meta {
  name: GetBarcodeResolved
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/npp/artikelscan?scan={{nppScanBarcode}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq resolved
  res.body.article.artnr: isString
  res.body.empty: eq false
}

docs {
  GET /web/npp/artikelscan?scan=<barcode> - step 3 of
  Luna.BusinessLogic.NPPArtikelScanBE:ResolveScan (no dash, no direct
  artnr/nummer match): the scan value is matched against artikel.barcode
  (artikel-x04) and/or art-subcodes.barcode (art-subcodes-x1). Exactly
  one candidate -> resolves directly, no "aantal" key.

  {{nppScanBarcode}} must be set (collection/environment variable, not
  currently in Local.bru) to a real artikel.barcode or art-subcodes.barcode
  value from LunaNew that maps to exactly ONE artnr, to exercise this
  single-candidate path (see GetMultipleCandidates.bru for the 2+ case).

  Read-only - backed by Backend/src/Luna/Web/NPPArtikelScanHandler.cls +
  Luna/BusinessLogic/NPPArtikelScanBE.cls.
}
